<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid DPS Phase 2</h2>Just as in Phase 1, item level remains the single most impactful attribute on any piece of gear in Phase 2, as it directly determines the total allocation of useful DPS stats on each item. This means that you can continue to use item level as an excellent proxy for DPS value when evaluating potential upgrades for your Feral Druid in Phase 2. The highest item level that is attainable from Phase 2 raid drops is 252 (from 25-man Hard Mode bosses in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a>), and unsurprisingly, the embedded BiS setup below uses a 252 item level piece in nearly every slot where one is available.<br/>
<br/>There are just two scenarios where deviating from maximum item level is optimal for Phase 2 gearing:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">The 2-piece bonus of the Tier 8 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-76/conquerors-nightsong-battlegear">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Nightsong Battlegear</span></a> set is worth a hefty 86 DPS in value from the extra <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=16870/clearcasting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_manaburn.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clearcasting</span></a> procs it provides, so it is worth giving up two higher item level off-pieces in order to accommodate this set bonus. The most efficient places to slot in two Tier 8 pieces are in the helm and glove slots, since there are no 252 item level Hard Mode options in those two slots. Note that the 4-piece Tier 8 bonus is quite weak by comparison, so it is not worth itemizing around it if you have access to Hard Mode loot.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> gear is overloaded in Hit Rating and Expertise Rating, so you will sometimes be forced to equip a lower item level piece in order to stay below the 8% Hit cap or 6.5% Expertise cap. For example, in the embedded BiS setup below, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46032/drape-of-the-faceless-general">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_14.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Drape of the Faceless General</span></a> is used instead of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45461/drape-of-icy-intent">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Drape of Icy Intent</span></a> due to its lack of Hit Rating, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45869/fluxing-energy-coils">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fluxing Energy Coils</span></a> are used in lieu of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45611/solar-bindings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_26.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solar Bindings</span></a> due to their lack of Expertise Rating.</div></li></ol>The only other change from Phase 1 gearing priorities is that Armor Penetration Rating will surpass Strength as the highest value DPS stat for Feral Druids once you are decked out in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> gear. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-stat-priority-attributes-pve">stat priority guide</a>, Armor Penetration scales rather uniquely among DPS stats in that it exhibits <i>increasing returns</i> in value, meaning that it becomes increasingly valuable as you accumulate more and more of it on your gear. The reason for this is because when the boss has very low residual armor, a loss of 1 additional armor is a more significant reduction in the boss's mitigation against your attacks than it is when the boss has a high amount of armor.<br/>
<br/>The main practical consequence of this increasing returns mechanic is that <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40002/fractured-scarlet-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Scarlet Ruby</span></a> gems will outperform <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39996/bold-scarlet-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Scarlet Ruby</span></a> gems once you accumulate enough Phase 2 upgrades to approach the Armor Penetration <i>soft cap</i>, which is the point at which a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40256/grim-toll">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Grim Toll</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a> proc will boost you to the maximum Armor Penetration Rating value of 1399. As a result, it is optimal to stack <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40002/fractured-scarlet-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Scarlet Ruby</span></a> gems in your gear set until you are just below the appropriate soft cap for your trinket setup, and then swap to <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39996/bold-scarlet-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Scarlet Ruby</span></a> gems for your remaining sockets. In the embedded BiS setup below with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a>, the soft cap for Armor Penetration Rating is 648, so the optimal configuration runs 602 Armor Penetration Rating from gear + gems, plus an additional 40 rating from a <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42995/hearty-rhino">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_food_115_condorsoup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hearty Rhino</span></a> food buff, in order to stay just below the soft cap.<br/>
<br/>With these gearing priorities in mind, shown below is the absolute highest DPS gear configuration that can be assembled by a Feral Druid in Phase 2:<br/>
