<br/>Note that the above BiS setup includes the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54999/hyperspeed-accelerators">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hyperspeed Accelerators</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55002/flexweave-underlay">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flexweave Underlay</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that it is assumed that any competitive Feral DPS player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed.<br/>
<br/>Also note that the displayed configuration is optimized for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> players. If you are an <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> Feral and are lucky enough to have a <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/draenei">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Draenei</span></a> in your party providing the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> buff, then simply swap out the two <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40014/rigid-autumns-glow">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_26.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Autumn's Glow</span></a> gems for <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40037/inscribed-monarch-topaz">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Monarch Topaz</span></a> gems instead, in order to stay below your reduced Hit cap of 7%.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Conquest for Feral Druid DPS Phase 2</h3>The only <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=221/emblem-of-conquest">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></span></a> reward in the BiS gear setup shown above is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45640/crown-of-the-wayward-vanquisher">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_24.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crown of the Wayward Vanquisher</span></a>, which can be exchanged for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46161/conquerors-nightsong-headguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Nightsong Headguard</span></a>. The other rewards are all outclassed by 10-man or 25-man raid drops, but can serve as solid intermediate upgrades while you are waiting for the BiS option to drop.<br/>
