<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Feral Druid DPS Phase 2</h3>The absolute best DPS trinket for Feral Druids in Phase 2 of WotLK is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a>, which provides a whopping 183 DPS boost relative to its Phase 1 counterpart <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40256/grim-toll">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Grim Toll</span></a>. Note that you should only ever equip one of these two trinkets in your gear set, since you will otherwise exceed the hard cap of 1399 Armor Penetration Rating when both trinket procs are active.<br/>
<br/>The optimal trinket to pair with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a> in the second trinket slot is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45609/comets-trail">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Comet's Trail</span></a> from 25-man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a>. However, since this trinket is likely to be extremely contested, a compromise option that will be more practical for most Ferals is to instead opt for its 10-man counterpart <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46038/dark-matter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_seedofdestruction.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Matter</span></a>, which is only 19 DPS worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45609/comets-trail">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Comet's Trail</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
