<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="idols-for-feral-druid-dps-phase-2">Idols for Feral Druid DPS Phase 2</h4>There are unfortunately no new cat DPS Idols from 10-man or 25-man raids in Phase 2, only <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45509/idol-of-the-corruptor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Corruptor</span></a> for bear tanking. As a result, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40713/idol-of-the-ravenous-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_idolofferocity.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Ravenous Beast</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39757/idol-of-worship">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Worship</span></a> will continue to be the only viable DPS options throughout Phase 2. Quite interestingly, due to the abundance of Armor Penetration Rating on <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> gear, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40713/idol-of-the-ravenous-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_idolofferocity.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Ravenous Beast</span></a> ends up performing better than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39757/idol-of-worship">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Worship</span></a> as a standalone Idol in simulations of Phase 2 BiS setups, since bonus <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48572/shred">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_vampiricaura.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shred</span></a> damage scales with Armor Penetration while bleed damage does not. However, just as in Phase 1, advanced players will be able to squeeze out even more DPS by using <i>both</i> of these Idols in tandem, swapping from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40713/idol-of-the-ravenous-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_idolofferocity.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Ravenous Beast</span></a> to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39757/idol-of-worship">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Worship</span></a> when you know that <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49800/rip">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_ghoulfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rip</span></a> will be falling off soon. As before, Idol swaps like this are best performed at the very end of a bearweave when shifting back into <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a>, in order to "cheat" the swing timer reset that is normally incurred whenever you swap weapons or Idols in combat.<div class="pad"></div>
